                <pb facs="0711" n="697" sameAs="frus:frus1950v06/pg697"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">751G.02/1–1950:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Thailand</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stanton</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bangkok</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-01-19T18:00:00+07:00">January 19, 1950—6
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>43. I believe Department under misapprehension re basic reason for reluctance
                    Thailand and probably other Southeast Asian countries extend recognition Bao
                    Dai. Basic reason is detestation by these countries of colonialism and their
                    repugnance voluntarily to recognize any regime which in their minds represents
                    perpetuation of colonial rule. It is my belief if French forthwith granted Bao
                    Dai real independence as Dutch have to Indos, there would be much less
                    reluctance to extend recognition. In my opinion this feeling is so strong in
                    their minds that it completely outweighs danger Ho Chi Minh establishing
                    Communist Government Indo-China. I believe veiled threats from US withhold
                    assistance these Asian countries would have little influence on their thinking
                    or the position they have adopted on this matter.</p>
                <p>Sent Department 43, pouched Rangoon, Manila, Jakarta, New Delhi, Saigon.
                    Department please repeat London, and Paris.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stanton</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
